# A definition's explicit read of its own node is not its free name. f reads
# n twice: bare, a free name, which a caller's value gives; and node\n, the
# value kept in the node its method built, which no caller changes. u5 is
# built with n 5. From the root, with no n: 5 and 5, 505. From outer, which
# has n 40: 40 and still 5, 4005. Entry 7.
fn: mk (int: n) fn: () int
    fn: f () int
        return: n * 100 + node\n
    return: f

u5: mk 5

fn: call5 () int
    return: u5()
end: call5

fn: outer () int
    int: n 40
    return: call5()
end: outer

int: a call5()
int: b outer()
int: ok 7
if: a != 505 || b != 4005
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
